Z||000000||KRMFiero||03-29-2001||03:53 PM||||My friend has a 1990 Jeep Wrangler (Nice) and the past few times we went off road we got stuck,  Examples:<P>1. Went over sand hill thing, chassie got stuck on top of sand hill and none of the tires were touching ground.<P>2. Yesturday we were going down a path 6-12" snow and we were crossing over a small pond and the ice cracked and it fell in (only the front) we were able to get it back but just it couldnt get traction on anything (Only 1 front wheel spins and 1 back wheel)<P>Anyways, he does not have a winch, he only has 29" tires, he does not have any lift kits on it.   What would you guys reccomend?  What should he get for a winch? do those Ball mount winches work good?  how many inches of lift should he get, should he aslo get a body lift? know any good places to by cheap winches, lifts, tires.  what size tires should he get  31/33/35's? what width?<P><BR>Thanks<BR>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
